WEBVTT

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.840
[Uhtred] <i>My name is Uhtred,</i>

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.840
<i>son of Uhtred.</i>

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.920
<i>I was born a Saxon,</i>

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
<i>but stolen, and raised as a Dane.</i>

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.560
<i>But now I find myself</i>

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.560
<i>bound to King Alfred.</i>

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.240
<i>And bound</i>

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.240
<i>by marriage to Wessex.</i>

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:25.040
<i>I have a Christian wife,</i>

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:25.040
<i>whom I care for.</i>

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.080
[baby crying]

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.240
<i>And I child I have never seen.</i>

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.200
<i>I have land,</i>

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.200
<i>burdened with debt.</i>

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.240
It is a substantial amount,

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.240
Lord.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.600
Alfred could remove the debt,

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.600
but he has chosen not to.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.120
[Uhtred] <i>And a sly servant</i>

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.120
<i>I cannot trust.</i>

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.120
<i>And though I miss</i>

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.120
<i>the ways of the Danes,</i>

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.480
<i>and their hunger for life</i>

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.480
<i>and for battle.</i>

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.400
Never cross Ubba.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.960
And never, never fight him.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:54.560
[Uhtred]<i> Fate has stirred</i>

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:54.560
<i>my Saxon heart for a reason.</i>

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.520
[man] <i>Ubba and his army</i>

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.520
<i>have returned from Ireland.</i>

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.680
And my fleet is where?

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.120
[man] <i>They left Lundene several</i>

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.120
<i>days ago and are nearly here, Lord.</i>

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.160
[Uhtred] <i>Destiny is all.</i>

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.840
[thunder rumbles]

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.880
[horse whinnies]

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:08.600
[Oswald]

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:08.600
Lord?

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:13.320
Lord?

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:13.320
When will you need assistance?

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.080
[baby crying]

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.680
Mildrith!

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.400
-Odda?

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.400
-Mildrith. Thank, God.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:28.200
-What are you doing here?

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:28.200
-You must come with me.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.160
The peace is over.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.160
We are under siege.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.040
Since when?

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.600
You must gather

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.600
all you need and quickly.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.280
The Danes could

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.280
be here at any time.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.120
-I cannot go with you.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.120
-Yes, you can. You must.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.200
If the peace is over,

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.200
then what of Uhtred?

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.560
Mildrith, the Danes

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.560
have broken the truce.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.240
We have killed

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.240
all the hostages given to us

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.600
and they will

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.600
have done the same.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.520
If Uhtred has survived,

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.280
it can only be as a traitor,

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.280
a Dane!

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:48.680
No.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.720
Regardless, it is no longer

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.720
safe for you here,

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.680
-you must come with me.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.680
-[thunder rumbles]

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.080
Mildrith! I beg you,

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.080
for the sake of your child.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.640
Do not worry about us lady,

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.960
we'll get ourselves and the

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.960
livestock to the hills.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.680
Get yourself

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.680
clear of this place.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.680
Anything of value I will bury!

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.720
[birds squawking]

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.440
[indistinct chatter]

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.560
[man] Don't just pull at the

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.560
bugger, you'll have it torn!

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:55.120
-Find out what holds it!

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:55.120
-[Uhtred] How much for your horse?

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.600
He's not for sale.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:09.040
I'll give you

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:09.040
twice its worth. In silver.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.520
Have any washed up alive?

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.320
Not on my beach.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.240
God's taken hundreds

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.240
of the bastards.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:26.200
Though it's said hundreds more have

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:26.200
landed safely, further up the shore.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.720
Friends of yours?

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:34.800
You should

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:34.800
take your families to safety.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:45.040
-Ertwit?

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:45.040
-He has your look, definitely.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.320
Little Ertwit. Little Ertwit.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.000
[chuckles]

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.960
Let's hope he does not

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.960
develop my constitution.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.920
[door opens]

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.640
They are here.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:00.000
Shh, shh, shh...

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:03.320
Odda? Wulfhere?

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.800
[both] Lord.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:08.600
Difficult times,

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:08.600
which we will face head on.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.080
Never rest.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.920
Do we march as one Lord,

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.920
or are we to split?

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.560
We are split.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.120
You both shall ride towards

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.120
the Severn River to face Ubba.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.720
I shall ride south

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.720
to face Guthrum.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:20.720
Should we not all be marching

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:20.720
to the Severn lord?

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.000
If this first battle is won,

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.560
then the Danes may not

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.560
care for a second.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.520
Wulfhere, even in victory

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.520
we can never be sure

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.960
of our surviving numbers.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:31.640
Some of Guthrum's ships

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:31.640
will of made it to shore,

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.440
and I can not let him simply

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.440
walk through Wessex;

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:35.800
he must be faced.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.520
Odda, should either of us

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.520
have luck

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:41.440
and defeat our enemy quickly,

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:41.440
we will march to the others aid.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.960
Yes, Lord, of course.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:44.640
Prepare...

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.400
[cows mooing]

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.400
[chickens clucking]

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.960
[man grunting]

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.720
By God, girl, you are a lovely

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.720
field to plough.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.840
A lovely field to plough.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:53.760
Better than barley...

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:53.760
Better than barley...

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:54.880
[grunts]

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:58.360
By God, girl,

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:58.360
better than barley!

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:01.240
Better than barley, yeah,

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.720
[screams]

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.840
Better than barley!

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:10.000
Lord! Lord! Forgive, Lord,

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:10.000
it's never happened before,

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:11.600
I swear it'll never

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:11.600
happen again.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:14.240
-It was the girl's idea.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:14.240
-It was not!

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.680
-Where's my wife?

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.680
-It was not my idea at--

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:19.160
-Where is my wife and child?

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:19.160
-Wait! Wait! Lord!

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:20.720
She's with

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:20.720
Lord Odda the Younger.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:22.040
-Odda?

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:22.040
-Yes, Lord.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.440
He took the lady and your son.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:25.360
She went willingly,

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:25.360
Lord, to protect the child.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.320
-My son?

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.320
-Yes, Lord, you have a son.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:33.320
Handsome little man he is.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:33.320
Looks like his father.

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.760
I should really take your balls

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.760
for this, desecration.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.920
Yes... No, Lor... Please.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.480
I do not care for you;

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.480
your wife,

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:40.640
your children nor your whore.

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:44.160
Lord, he made me do it,

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:44.160
with the promise of a coin.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.320
It was false promise, Lord,

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.320
I have no coin.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.720
I will need a fresh horse,

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.720
food and drink.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:53.560
Yes, Lord. Your own horse was

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:53.560
returned, it's in the stable.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.360
My house is not your house.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:57.560
No, Lord.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:57.560
I beg your pardon, Lord.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:59.960
My land is not your land.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:02.800
Treat me as a fool again

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:02.800
and I'll kill you.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.240
Yes, Lord.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:06.240
I'll enjoy it.

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:08.320
I believe you would.

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:24.560
Leave me.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:40.240
Uhtred... son of Uhtred...

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.760
We outnumber them I feel.

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:19.240
[Leofric]

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:19.240
We outnumber them if you count

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.240
the farm boys and women, Lord.

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:23.560
You fear them, Leofric?

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:26.160
I do not. Though some do.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:28.000
It is not about fear,

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:28.000
it is about strategy.

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:31.040
We hold the high ground;

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:31.040
they must come to us.

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:32.200
And if they

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:32.200
decide to wait, Lord?

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:33.760
Why would they?

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:36.320
Because we are sat isolated

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:36.320
on this high ground.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:37.400
[Wulfhere] And supplies are low.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:39.200
They don't know that!

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:43.800
We bide our time.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:43.800
Hold our position.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:46.920
With luck,

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:46.920
Alfred will see off Guthrum,

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.760
and provide us

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.760
with reinforcements.

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:55.360
For now we stay put... on this hill.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.680
[indistinct chatter]

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:19.200
Lord...

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:21.720
They are gathering,

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:21.720
and they are watching.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:23.640
They have the higher ground.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:26.480
But I do not want to wait.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:32.160
So... when do I attack?

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.440
I'll cast the runes.

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:38.840
Storri,

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:38.840
I will need a clear answer.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.320
I will get one.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:51.600
[spits]

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:07.200
I have your answer, Lord.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:12.440
Look, this is us

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:12.440
at the base of their hill,

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:14.200
they sit on top,

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:17.920
but that's not an advantage.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:24.800
This is a feather from that

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:24.800
camp, bone dry and faded.

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:31.280
Water runs down the hill,

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:31.280
not up.

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:34.560
You have your wish, Lord,

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:34.560
an early attack is good.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.360
They're weak.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:39.760
They will surrender or die,

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:44.840
and then we move into

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:44.840
the heart of Wessex.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:48.040
Shield wall!

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:53.880
Advance!

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:56.440
-One! Two!

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:56.440
-[men grunt in unison]

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:59.200
-[man] Horsemen approaching!

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:59.200
-Halt.

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:03.480
[yelling in distance]

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:15.320
Go and fetch, Lord Odda...

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:17.680
...the Elder!

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:28.400
It is Uhtred...

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:28.400
How could he have lived?

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.640
We will ask.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:32.720
Aelderman Uhtred,

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:32.720
we feared you'd been killed!

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:35.600
That you were not is a miracle,

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:35.600
or something less godly.

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:37.000
[grunting]

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:38.280
-Where is she?

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:38.280
-What? What?

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:39.760
Where's my wife and child?

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:41.280
-She... she's safe!

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:41.280
-You brought her here?!

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.720
She is safe!

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.720
Did you not hear him!?

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:44.320
She is safe! I took her

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:44.320
to safety, nothing more!

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:48.160
Mildrith is with my own wife!

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:48.160
On my land, in my house!

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.320
Where she has lived

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.320
happily in the past!

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:51.640
Put away your dagger!

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:53.400
Swear that you haven't

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:53.400
laid a hand on her.

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:55.480
-I will do no such thing!

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:55.480
-Swear!

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:59.920
Lord you will take your blade

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.480
away from my Lord

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.480
and you will do it now.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.520
Arseling!

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:11.280
You have my word that neither Mildrith

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:11.280
nor your son have been harmed.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.640
I swear, do as I ask.

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:18.200
[panting]

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.160
Treason...

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.160
but what can we expect.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:26.440
Enough, this in-fighting

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:26.440
and argument!

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:30.040
Disperse... all of you! Now!

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:35.720
Your wife remains

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:35.720
my goddaughter.

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:38.200
You should be thanking my son,

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:38.200
not threatening him!

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:40.200
Now come to me

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:40.200
when your thinking is clear.

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:44.920
And you explain to me why you are

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:44.920
still breathing... and stupid!

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:51.920
You are back from the dead

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:51.920
and unchanged.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.040
All you had to do

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.040
was get down from your horse

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:56.720
and ask,

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:56.720
"Have you seen my wife?"

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:04.320
That would have been

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:04.320
the better choice, yes,

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:09.040
but then Young Odda

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:09.040
wouldn't have shit himself.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.480
[both laughing]

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:16.120
You seen her? She's well?

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.200
She is well.

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:19.160
The child, however...

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:21.000
-Sickly?

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:21.000
-Ugly.

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:21.960
Like his father?

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:25.400
Worse... with the smallest

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:25.400
of pebbles for a penis.

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:27.360
Like his father.

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:29.160
[chuckling]

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:31.440
If you wish to see him

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:31.440
for yourself, Arseling,

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:33.040
I say you leave

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:33.040
the way you came.

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:34.920
I'm serious.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:38.360
We are stuck on

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:38.360
this hill and here we will die.

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:40.160
What does Odda say?

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:44.040
Odda is a decent man,

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:44.040
but as a warrior,

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:46.720
he has all the guile

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:46.720
and menace of a sheep.

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:52.360
[Odda the Elder]

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:52.360
We have the ground; the slope...

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:54.760
I will not surrender

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:54.760
that advantage.

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:56.800
But if food is scarce, Lord,

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:56.800
how long can we wait?

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:58.200
We shall find food!

00:14:58.280 --> 00:14:59.800
We have food for how many days?

00:14:58.280 --> 00:14:59.800
Two, three, four?

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:02.040
Enough time

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:02.040
for Alfred to arrive.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:03.840
You yourself have reported

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.680
that the storm has taken

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.680
most of Guthrum's ships.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:08.680
-But not all.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:08.680
-But enough, perhaps...

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.720
So we wait. Mm?

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:14.920
Agreed, for a time.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:18.080
We give Alfred

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:18.080
as much time as possible.

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:23.760
I will offer negotiations,

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:25.440
and while those negotiations

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:25.440
are taking place

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:28.200
we will send out

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:28.200
hunting parties, several.

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:32.680
Alfred will come.

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:37.120
I'll attend

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:37.120
these negotiations with Ubba.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:39.040
You have not been invited.

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.120
It's my right.

00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:01.160
If the other hostages

00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:01.160
were killed, how did he survive?

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:04.640
He was taken as a child

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:04.640
by the Danes and he survived.

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:06.280
We would do well to follow him.

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.480
Follow him?

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:13.120
Or listen to what he has to say,

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:13.120
Lord, is what I meant.

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:35.960
Lord Ubba, may I present

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:35.960
the Lord Odda of Wessex.

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:39.040
There never seems to be a

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:39.040
meeting that you do not attend.

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:42.120
Is there more than one of you?

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:46.200
Lord Ubba, Odda's Alfred's

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:46.200
most trusted general.

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:48.200
[scoffs]

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:50.840
I don't give a shit who he is,

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:54.520
all he needs to do is to surrender.

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:56.120
There will be no surrender.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.560
[chuckles]

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.560
What will there be?

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:02.160
There will be no surrender.

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:06.160
Though I do invite you

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:06.160
to return to your ships.

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:07.800
Guthrum may have

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:07.800
broken the peace,

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.960
but there's no need

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.960
for Ubba to do likewise.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:13.840
We will not be

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:13.840
returning to our ships.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:15.240
And I shall not be moving

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:15.240
from this hill.

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:16.560
[chuckles]

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:17.960
You have

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:17.960
no business in Wessex.

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:20.760
My business is to kill you.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:26.400
-You may try.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:26.400
-Guthrum's fleet's gone.

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:28.800
Njord reached out from the deep

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:31.760
and dragged Guthrum's fleet

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:31.760
down to the sea-bed.

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:33.640
You're lying.

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:35.960
I watched the fleet die

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:35.960
and its men go under!

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:37.760
Storri, what do you say?!

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:41.800
Lord, I do not see for Guthrum,

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:41.800
I... I see for you.

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:43.280
Storri is a man who wears

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:43.280
a stick up his arse,

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:44.840
he didn't

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:44.840
see that coming either.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:47.240
No, that... that's a lie.

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:48.920
It's all lies! Look at his eyes!

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.520
You are next to die, Ubba,

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.520
and I know it, I cast the runes.

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:52.720
That's an even bigger lie.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:54.520
Earl Ragnar the Fearless

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:54.520
is with the Gods

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:55.760
and they are angry at you;

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.640
you allow his death

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.640
to go unpunished.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:01.120
Avenging Earl Ragnar

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:01.120
is not my business!

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:02.440
That's for his son!

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:03.840
You're next to die, Ubba.

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:05.480
[yells]

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:09.520
Then fight me! And you'll see

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:09.520
who is next to die! Fight me!

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:12.640
Lord... we're negotiating.

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:14.360
You will not say another word!

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:16.560
He will not say another word!

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:18.840
He will not, no. Best not.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:25.320
I will not say another word.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:25.320
Talking is over.

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:29.920
You piece of weasel shit!

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:36.920
Storri! Storri!

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:49.240
[exhales]

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:52.280
What now?

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:53.880
Where we left standing? In shit?

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:55.080
Now we have time.

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:56.560
How? If it were possible,

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:57.960
you've made them

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:57.960
want to kill us even more!

00:18:58.040 --> 00:18:59.960
We should attack.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:11.360
[indistinct chatter]

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:39.960
[men laughing]

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:55.400
[Odda the Elder]

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:55.400
My men are good men.

00:19:57.640 --> 00:20:02.520
Though half of them are armed only

00:19:57.640 --> 00:20:02.520
with reaping hooks, they're here.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:09.080
Reaping hooks can kill.

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:14.960
How well do you know Ubba?

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:18.040
I've known Ubba

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:18.040
since I was 11-years-old.

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:23.440
He is the greatest warrior

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:23.440
I have ever seen,

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:28.000
but he's cautious, he listens

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:28.000
to the gods, always.

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:31.160
I goaded him

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:31.160
only to make him doubt.

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:33.760
It will take a little while

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:33.760
for the doubt to clear,

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:37.680
you have your time, but I say again,

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:37.680
we should attack.

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:39.920
If we attack

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:39.920
we will be outflanked,

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:45.640
my men die, all of them.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:45.640
I know each of them.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:53.560
I'd hoped this hill and Alfred

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:53.560
might save them... us.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:55.720
Alfred won't come.

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:58.080
The food won't last,

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:58.080
and Ubba's mind will clear.

00:20:58.160 --> 00:21:02.400
It seems inevitable,

00:20:58.160 --> 00:21:02.400
they will take Wessex.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:05.960
What if we were able

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:05.960
to outflank the Danes?

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:07.880
How?

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:09.920
We burn their ships.

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:13.160
Even if it's just three or four,

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:14.680
they'd be running to the fire.

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:17.280
-Then we attack.

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:17.280
-They'll be disorganized.

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.080
No shield wall.

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:21.320
We could be killing them

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:21.320
before they know we're there.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.880
Who would set the fires?

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:27.960
I will. Alone.

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:30.680
But I'll need your word

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:33.880
that you'll attack as soon

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:33.880
as the fires have taken hold.

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:38.320
You have it.

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:43.120
If we succeed, Lord,

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:43.120
you'll have saved Wessex.

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:19.640
If he succeeds,

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:19.640
fires the ships,

00:22:19.720 --> 00:22:22.640
it will undoubtedly cause panic

00:22:19.720 --> 00:22:22.640
amongst the Danes.

00:22:22.720 --> 00:22:24.480
Which is the aim.

00:22:24.560 --> 00:22:27.800
How best do we use that panic?

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:35.520
Is an attack

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:35.520
likely to be successful?

00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:42.040
Would it not be better

00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:42.040
to escape this hill?

00:22:42.840 --> 00:22:44.840
We can return to Winchester

00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:46.800
without the loss

00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:46.800
of a single man.

00:22:46.880 --> 00:22:49.640
Excepting Uhtred.

00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:56.120
Father, if what Uhtred says

00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:56.120
about the storm is true,

00:22:56.680 --> 00:22:59.600
and Guthrum's fleet

00:22:56.680 --> 00:22:59.600
is all but destroyed,

00:22:59.680 --> 00:23:02.920
we would

00:22:59.680 --> 00:23:02.920
join forces with Alfred;

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:06.640
we may well meet him

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:06.640
on the road.

00:23:07.800 --> 00:23:10.120
Then we are all against Ubba.

00:23:12.280 --> 00:23:15.040
As a strategy it makes sense.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:30.400
I gave him my word.

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:35.720
He will die,

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:35.720
and you can call him a hero.

00:23:37.640 --> 00:23:43.760
The others are here, you must

00:23:37.640 --> 00:23:43.760
decide what you will tell them.

00:23:55.960 --> 00:23:56.960
I have called for you,

00:23:57.040 --> 00:24:01.920
to tell you to ready your men;

00:23:57.040 --> 00:24:01.920
all men. Everyone.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:05.280
-We shall be moving... soon.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:05.280
-Moving, Lord?

00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:08.560
Aelderman Uhtred, has volunteered

00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:08.560
himself to distract the Danes.

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:10.520
He will endeavor to set alight

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:10.520
a number of their ships.

00:24:10.600 --> 00:24:11.960
-He has gone?

00:24:10.600 --> 00:24:11.960
-Yes.

00:24:12.040 --> 00:24:14.040
-Alone?

00:24:12.040 --> 00:24:14.040
-Yes.

00:24:14.120 --> 00:24:17.680
If he should succeed

00:24:14.120 --> 00:24:17.680
in causing this distraction,

00:24:17.760 --> 00:24:19.000
we will move.

00:24:19.080 --> 00:24:21.280
In which direction, Lord?

00:24:21.360 --> 00:24:23.680
Ready your men;

00:24:21.360 --> 00:24:23.680
tell them nothing.

00:24:23.760 --> 00:24:25.640
Lord Odda, with respect,

00:24:23.760 --> 00:24:25.640
you told us nothing.

00:24:25.720 --> 00:24:27.120
I have told you

00:24:25.720 --> 00:24:27.120
to ready your men.

00:24:27.200 --> 00:24:30.880
-Ready for battle?

00:24:27.200 --> 00:24:30.880
-Ready your men, each of you.

00:24:30.960 --> 00:24:34.160
Go! Prepare!

00:24:49.120 --> 00:24:51.200
[indistinct chatter]

00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:15.000
[laughing]

00:25:51.360 --> 00:25:53.000
[grunts]

00:27:05.080 --> 00:27:07.600
I see nothing on the river.

00:27:11.280 --> 00:27:15.480
-It will soon be first light.

00:27:11.280 --> 00:27:15.480
-Can you not speak?

00:27:20.480 --> 00:27:22.280
Very well.

00:27:22.360 --> 00:27:24.880
[flames cackling]

00:27:29.360 --> 00:27:34.360
Ships afire! Ships afire!

00:27:34.440 --> 00:27:37.320
[indistinct shouting]

00:27:37.400 --> 00:27:40.160
Fetch buckets and barrels!

00:27:51.080 --> 00:27:53.280
[men yelling]

00:28:21.720 --> 00:28:25.920
Lord Odda, we are ready,

00:28:21.720 --> 00:28:25.920
but to do what?

00:28:30.680 --> 00:28:32.480
He's done it.

00:28:33.440 --> 00:28:35.880
Look, he's fired the ships.

00:28:40.720 --> 00:28:42.360
We attack!

00:28:42.440 --> 00:28:45.080
Lord? Lord you awake?

00:28:46.480 --> 00:28:47.680
-Lord!

00:28:46.480 --> 00:28:47.680
-What?

00:28:47.760 --> 00:28:48.960
The ships have been fired!

00:28:49.040 --> 00:28:51.240
[groans]

00:28:55.120 --> 00:28:57.280
-It's him, I know it!

00:28:55.120 --> 00:28:57.280
-Yes.

00:28:57.360 --> 00:29:01.360
You saw them dying on the hill!

00:28:57.360 --> 00:29:01.360
Did you not see a fire?!

00:29:01.440 --> 00:29:03.520
I told you I can only see

00:29:01.440 --> 00:29:03.520
what the runes allow!

00:29:03.600 --> 00:29:06.040
-How many ships burn?

00:29:03.600 --> 00:29:06.040
-I don't know. Many.

00:29:06.120 --> 00:29:08.600
They are planning something,

00:29:06.120 --> 00:29:08.600
they must be.

00:29:19.680 --> 00:29:22.720
Lord... there.

00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:24.160
That's him.

00:29:25.640 --> 00:29:30.080
You! Uhtred Ragnarson! You!

00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:34.040
Are you afraid of me?

00:29:34.120 --> 00:29:39.600
Man on man,

00:29:34.120 --> 00:29:39.600
I will make the square.

00:29:41.720 --> 00:29:44.760
Will you fight me?

00:29:45.440 --> 00:29:49.280
Are you the son of

00:29:45.440 --> 00:29:49.280
Ragnar the Fearless?

00:29:50.600 --> 00:29:54.640
Or are you a coward?!

00:30:10.720 --> 00:30:13.400
I will fight you Ubba,

00:30:10.720 --> 00:30:13.400
if that's what you want,

00:30:14.240 --> 00:30:15.840
but you will die.

00:30:16.960 --> 00:30:18.720
Fetch him a shield.

00:30:26.680 --> 00:30:29.240
You are half naked, Lord,

00:30:26.680 --> 00:30:29.240
you might catch a chill.

00:30:29.600 --> 00:30:32.040
This will not take long.

00:30:41.680 --> 00:30:44.240
Was it you? The fires?

00:30:46.680 --> 00:30:51.240
Must have been the gods...

00:30:46.680 --> 00:30:51.240
they're angry with you.

00:31:03.800 --> 00:31:05.640
First blood or to the death?

00:31:05.720 --> 00:31:11.000
-[yells]

00:31:05.720 --> 00:31:11.000
-[all yelling]

00:31:13.400 --> 00:31:15.720
[grunting]

00:31:32.800 --> 00:31:34.800
Get up! Get up!

00:31:39.360 --> 00:31:41.440
[grunting]

00:31:48.160 --> 00:31:50.440
[groans in pain]

00:32:02.960 --> 00:32:05.520
[yells indistinct]

00:32:06.840 --> 00:32:09.440
[grunts]

00:32:21.640 --> 00:32:24.040
[shouts in pain]

00:32:46.280 --> 00:32:48.920
Go to Valhalla, Lord...

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:50.720
[grunts]

00:32:55.960 --> 00:32:59.000
[panting]

00:33:24.000 --> 00:33:27.000
[Leofric]

00:33:24.000 --> 00:33:27.000
Shield... wall!

00:33:28.640 --> 00:33:34.400
-Now kill the bastards!

00:33:28.640 --> 00:33:34.400
-[all shouting]

00:33:45.760 --> 00:33:48.880
[birds squawking]

00:33:48.960 --> 00:33:50.680
[Odda the Younger]

00:33:48.960 --> 00:33:50.680
Tie them...

00:33:50.760 --> 00:33:55.000
Tie them all together,

00:33:50.760 --> 00:33:55.000
form a chain.

00:33:55.080 --> 00:33:56.760
Bind them tightly.

00:33:56.840 --> 00:34:00.680
If any object,

00:33:56.840 --> 00:34:00.680
march them into the river.

00:34:03.520 --> 00:34:05.800
Get this

00:34:03.520 --> 00:34:05.800
inside your belly, arseling.

00:34:10.320 --> 00:34:12.240
God knows you deserve it.

00:34:21.640 --> 00:34:26.280
Lord Odda is hurt... badly.

00:34:29.120 --> 00:34:30.640
He kept his word.

00:34:30.720 --> 00:34:35.640
He would, he is a good man;

00:34:35.720 --> 00:34:37.400
a good Aelderman.

00:34:37.480 --> 00:34:39.920
I want Ubba buried

00:34:37.480 --> 00:34:39.920
with his axe.

00:34:40.000 --> 00:34:41.600
His axe is gone.

00:34:42.480 --> 00:34:44.040
Young Odda wants him

00:34:42.480 --> 00:34:44.040
cut into pieces.

00:34:44.120 --> 00:34:46.720
-No, that can't happen.

00:34:44.120 --> 00:34:46.720
-He would have done the same to you.

00:34:46.800 --> 00:34:49.520
He is Ubba, as close as the

00:34:46.800 --> 00:34:49.520
Danes will ever come to a king.

00:34:51.360 --> 00:34:53.400
